   262	* The partitions in (3.3) are numerical germ-signature partitions.  They
   263	  do not count analytic moduli or locations, do not group germs into global
   264	  carrier curves, and are not quotiented by the stabilizer of the chosen
   265	  diagram representative.
   266	
   267	Every `n` has the unit-vertex partition consisting of `n_i` copies of
   268	`e_i`.  Consequently the maximum possible germ number is `w(n)`, with
   269	coefficient one.  A one-germ partition exists exactly when `n` itself has
   270	support on one vertex, or on both endpoints of one edge and nowhere else.
   271	The congruence (1.2) or (1.4) still applies to the total `n`; an individual
   272	branch need not separately be a Cartier divisor downstairs.
