   371	## 6. Forest topology uses physical germs, not `n`
   372	
   373	Take a full embedded log resolution of the reduced first-leg boundary.  Over
   374	one singular point, include in `T_p` the ADE tree and every additional
   375	exceptional vertex introduced to resolve its boundary contacts.  It is a
   376	connected tree.  Delete the interior of `T_p` from the resolved dual graph.
   377	Then the exact forest criterion is:
   378	
   379	> Every connected component of the remaining graph may meet `T_p` by at
   380	> most one edge.                                                   (6.1)
   381	
   382	Indeed two such edges, together with the unique path inside `T_p` and a path
   383	inside that outside component, form a cycle.  Conversely, attaching forest
   384	components once to a tree preserves a forest.
   385	
   386	The edges in (6.1) are distinct **physical branch contacts after log
   387	resolution**.  They are not the integers `n_i`.
   388	
   389	Consequently the forest kills:
   390	
   391	* two distinct physical branches of one irreducible strict different
   392	  component attaching to the same exceptional tree;
   393	* attachments from two vertices or points whose carriers are already joined
   394	  by a boundary path outside that tree; and
   395	* two disjoint connector loci between the connected total transforms of
   396	  infinity and of the different, unless those supports share a component
   397	  that changes the quotient graph.
   398	
   399	It does not kill:
   400	
   401	* one tangent branch with `n_i>1` at a single physical point;
   402	* one branch through an ADE node, with `n` supported on the two adjacent
   403	  vertices; or
   404	* several branches on distinct outside components which are connected only
   405	  through `T_p`, producing a star rather than a cycle.
   406	
   407	There is a useful global formulation.  In a forest, two connected subgraphs
   408	have connected intersection after subdividing physical intersection points
   409	as vertices.  The support of `H` is connected because it is an effective
   410	ample `(2,3)` divisor on the infinity surface `P1 times P1`; the support of
   411	`R_X` is connected because `2A+B` is ample on `X`.  Their total transforms
   412	are therefore connected.  A survivor with no shared nonexceptional carrier
   413	has only one graph-theoretic connector between them.  The eight units in
   414	`H.R=8` may nevertheless concentrate at that connector as tangency or ADE
   415	Cartier multiplicity.  Numerical weight eight is not eight graph edges.
