   448	## 8. Hostile checks, exact remaining gap, and scope firewall
   449	
   450	The following tempting shortcuts are false and have been excluded from the
   451	theorem.
   452	
   453	* **Rank at most nine allows `E6` or `E7`.**  The signed-coordinate proof in
   454	  Section 2 uses the actual roots of `D9`, not rank alone, and removes them.
   455	* **`n_i=4` means four boundary edges.**  It can be one order-four physical
   456	  contact.  Forest topology sees the resolved branch path.
   457	* **Support on two ADE vertices means two physical points.**  A branch
   458	  through their node gives one point, as in the even `A_r` survivor (3.5).
   459	* **Every congruence solution occurs.**  Equations (3.1) and (4.2) are only
   460	  the Cartier-lattice gate.  The effective cone and analytic incidence map
   461	  remain unproved.
   462	* **`A.R=8` always bounds `sum n`.**  The proof needs a pullback line meeting
   463	  the different properly.  It can fail at a nonfinite coefficient basepoint.
   464	* **Connected infinity and different must meet transversely many times.**
   465	  In a forest their entire intersection must instead collapse to one
   466	  connector; all eight intersection units may be concentrated there.
   467	* **A common infinity/different carrier has nonnegative residual
   468	  intersection.**  Proper intersection has failed, so (5.6) cannot be used.
   469	
   470	The exact remaining finite task in the projectively finite,
   471	no-common-carrier stratum is to enumerate the pairs
   472	
   473	```text
   474	(a,n) in (C Z^r intersect (Z_(>=0)^r minus {0}))^2,
   475	sum n_i<=8,       a^t C^(-1)n<=8,                   (8.1)
   476	```
   477	
   478	together with their partitions into physical analytic branches, the single-
   479	connector forest condition, simultaneous embeddings of all singular trees
   480	in `D9`, and effectivity of the strict carrier classes in the ruled
   481	nine-blowup marking.  Formula (8.1) is finite and exact, but this packet does
   482	not assert that every pair is realized.
   483	
   484	Separately unresolved are: a different component contained in infinity; a
   485	vertical/base fibre contained in the different; projective or affine
   486	coefficient-basepoint nonfiniteness; the local analytic restriction imposed
